==German==

===Etymology===
{{dercat|de|gmw-pro}}
From a conflation of.

* {{inh|de|gmh|anelich}}, {{m|gmh|enlich|t=alike; similar}}, from {{inh|de|goh|anagilih}}, from {{m|goh|ana}} + {{m|goh|gilih}} and
* {{inh|de|gmh|einlich}}, {{m|gmh|enlich|t=uniform; consistent}}, ultimately from {{der|de|gem-pro|*ana}} + {{m|gem-pro|*galīkaz}}.

Cognate with {{cog|dum|aenlijck}}, {{cog|enm|anlike}}, {{m|enm|anlyke}}, {{m|enm|anlich}}, {{m|enm|onlich}}, {{cog|non|álíkr}}. More at {{l|en|alike}}; {{l|en|only}}.

